            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">A 60-year-old man with relapsing unstable angina a year aftger an anterior acute myocardial infarction treated with PCI to proximal left anterior descending (LAD) and proximal intermediate branch (IB), resulting in a severely impaired LV function.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INVESTIGATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Physical examination, laboratorytest, transthoracic echocardiogram, rest ECG, coronary angiography.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DIAGNOSIS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Severe in-stent restenosis to IB, with a bulky plaque involving distal left main, obtuse marginal and proximal circumflex.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MANAGEMENT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Percutaneous coronary intervention/coronary artery bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
